WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.680
A winter night over the sea.

2
00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.790
One star hangs high above the snowy hills,

3
00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:07.610
and it never moves.

4
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.900
A young poet looks up and
makes a wish: "Bright Star,

5
00:00:11.950 --> 00:00:14.830
would I were steadfast as thou art".

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.650
Eight lines later, one
word cuts the wish in two.

7
00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:19.550
No.

8
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.710
He wanted to be like the star.

9
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.340
So why does he suddenly say no?

10
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.690
In this mission, you'll meet
John Keats, and Fanny Brawne,

11
00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.200
the neighbour he loved.

12
00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:31.750
You'll watch what the star does all night:

13
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.720
gazing at the sea, and
the snow on the moors.

14
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:38.510
And you'll find where this
sonnet turns, at line 9.

15
00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: work out why he says no.
